# No build-time PUBLIC_ configuration is required for the forms or the anti-abuse challenge any
# more. Both forms post to our own `/api/forms` Pages Function, and the anti-abuse challenge is a
# self-hosted proof-of-work issued by our own `/api/challenge` Pages Function — there is no
# third-party form backend, no site key, and nothing that must be baked into the client bundle.
# (Formspree and Cloudflare Turnstile, which used to be configured here, are gone.)
#
# All configuration for those paths is SERVER-side and lives with the Pages project instead:
# see the NOTE blocks in wrangler.toml (ALTCHA_HMAC_SECRET, EMAIL_API_TOKEN, EMAIL_ACCOUNT_ID,
# FORMS_FROM_ADDRESS / FORMS_DELIVERY_ADDRESS).
#
# PUBLIC_DIST_CHANNEL (web | ios | android) is set by the build pipeline per channel, not here.
